.TH BOSWAS-COMPOSITOR 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-compositor \- the Boswas OS display server and window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-compositor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-compositor
is the display server, window manager and effects engine of the Boswas OS
desktop. It draws every window and its frame (title bar, caption buttons,
rounded corners, shadow), animates windows and desktops, routes all input,
and decides which program may see or control what. Applications connect to
it with the standard Wayland protocols; X11 applications run through the
X server it starts for them.
.PP
It is normally started by
.BR boswas-session (1).
Once it accepts clients it starts the shell
.RB ( boswas-shell (1))
as a trusted client and restarts it if it exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " KIND"
\fBudev\fR: real hardware (DRM/KMS, libinput, libseat); the default on a
virtual terminal.
\fBwinit\fR: a window inside another Wayland or X11 session; the default
there.
\fBheadless\fR: one output rendered in software into memory, for tests.
.TP
.BI \-\-headless\-size " WIDTH" x HEIGHT
Size of the headless output (default 1920x1080).
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " NAME"
Wayland socket name (default: the first free \fBwayland\-\fIN\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read only this configuration file instead of the layers below.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shell
Do not start the shell.
.TP
.B \-\-test\-input
Accept input-injection commands on trusted control connections. For tests.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-env
Print \fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR and \fBBOSWAS_COMPOSITOR_SOCKET\fR on standard
output once the compositor is ready.
.TP
.BI \-\-send " COMMAND"
Send a command to a running compositor's control socket, print the reply
and exit: \fBversion\fR, \fBlock\fR, \fBreload\-config\fR, \fBoutputs\fR or
\fBcapture\fR. With \fB\-\-control\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR another
compositor's socket is used.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
